1,Mwimbi-Muthambi | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/mws,mws ISO 639. Mwimbi-Muthambi. Summary. Mwimbi-Muthambi is a stable indigenous language of Kenya. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Mwimbi-Muthambi,Niger-Congo
